From f4038e6755e6f17869b71c7d00ca813b0d218fd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:43:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0243: walk the global heap list for the FrameHeap arena-grow
 overflow (replace array[0]-only lookup)

0242 tried array[0] only, but the V1.3.65 device run proved array[0]'s allocate (0x951dc0, vtable 0xdbdae0) fails for the 946,368-byte Football SARC and calls V (log-121c8fb1.txt: backtrace main+0x97bfd4 main+0x951f54 main+0x14d425c -- frame 4 is 0x14d425c, the return after the 0242 trampoline's ALLOCATE blr, and frame 3 is 0x951f54, the return after the call to V inside 0x951dc0's late grow site 0x951f50). 0x951dc0 is a free-list ExpHeap allocate; its free list has no 946,368-byte block.

The key problem for a traversal: both the FrameHeap allocator (0x954310) and the ExpHeap allocate (0x951dc0) call V (abort) on failure instead of returning 0 -- they return 0 only if [S] == 0 or [S+0x10] == 0. So the trampoline NULLs [S+0x10] first (saving it at [sp,#0x00]) and restores it on both exits; a failed allocate then returns 0 and the loop tries the next heap. The walk skips NULL entries and any heap whose vtable IS the FrameHeap vtable (0xdbdf00), tries each heap's vtable+0x30 allocate, and falls back to V if none works. Loop state across the blr: x24 (current array pointer) and [sp,#0x38] (remaining count); the grow request at [sp,#8]-[sp,#0x28] is untouched. The [heap_iface+0x48] parent-heap candidate is subsumed (any registered parent is tried by the walk). Mock 0243diag-harness: ALL CHECKS PASSED (old 0242 reproduces the V1.3.65 abort via the late grow site; new 0243 returns a pointer from the second heap). Asm test-0243-asm.py: ALL CHECKS PASSED (38 instructions, clean decode).
